  "body": "Requested by the maintainer (2026-11-10): \"please make the small changes for unification. We do not want double code and make this confusing.\"\n\nFollow-up to #748/#749 (PRs #750, #751), which moved the local gate and release cut into `cargo xtask` but left the GitHub workflows and some docs as they were.\n\n## Double code today\n1. **Windows portable zip layout exists twice:** inline PowerShell in `.github/workflows/release.yml` (Windows job, \"Assemble portable zip\" + the installer built from the same staged tree) and `xtask/src/release_pack.rs` (`cargo xtask release`). Nothing keeps them in step.\n2. **`ci.yml` / `nightly.yml`** call `./scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier batch|release`, which is now a wrapper around `cargo xtask gate`.\n3. **`scripts/README.md`'s gate section** still documents `powershell -File scripts/gate.ps1 ...` as the command, and says batch/release run in \"push/PR CI\" / \"nightly CI\" (both are manual-only now).\n4. **The process-file lists are incomplete.** The AGENTS.md fork-sync list and review-prs step 2d omit the wrappers `scripts/release.ps1` and `scripts/collect-decisions.ps1`/`.sh`.\n\n## Change\n- **`cargo xtask package --version X.Y.Z [--out dist] [--bin-dir <dir>]`:** stages the portable tree and writes the zip, nothing else (no bump, no commit, no build). Both `cargo xtask release` (its zip phase) and `release.yml`'s Windows job call it. The installer step consumes the staged tree xtask reports. The layout lives once, in `release_pack.rs`, pinned by its existing unit test.\n- **`ci.yml` and `nightly.yml`:** run `cargo xtask gate batch` / `cargo xtask gate release` directly. Triggers and the OS matrix are unchanged: still `workflow_dispatch` only (Actions budget).\n- **`scripts/README.md`:** the gate section is rewritten around `cargo xtask gate` (Windows/macOS/Linux examples), wrappers mentioned once, and the CI wording corrected.\n- **The process-file lists** (AGENTS.md fork sync, review-prs 2d) add `scripts/release.ps1` and `scripts/collect-decisions.ps1`/`.sh`. PROCESS_VERSION bump.\n\n## Done means\n- One zip layout in the repo: `release.yml` has no inline staging block; a test pins the staged file list; `cargo xtask package --dry-run` (or a real run into a temp dir) on Windows produces the same tree the workflow's old block did. That's checked by diffing the file lists, recorded in the PR.\n- `ci.yml`/`nightly.yml` call `cargo xtask gate`, still manual-only.\n- `scripts/README.md` and the process-file lists name the xtask commands; no doc presents a wrapper as the primary command.\n- Not exercisable before a tag: `release.yml` itself. The PR says so, and the next `vX.Y.0` tag is its first run.\n",
